GACODE (TGLF, NEO, VGEN, EXPRO) — Apache License 2.0
===============================================================================

MITIM's in-process transport interfaces, in

    src/mitim_tools/simulation_tools/interfaces/

are built against GACODE (https://github.com/gafusion/gacode), which is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. GACODE sources are NOT
redistributed with MITIM: the build scripts compile them from the user's own
GACODE_ROOT installation, and the Python layer loads GACODE's own input
parsers from that installation at runtime.

The following file is a derivative work of GACODE and remains under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

    src/mitim_tools/simulation_tools/interfaces/vgen_c_api.f90
        Derived from gacode/vgen/src/vgen.f90.
        Modifications: MPI parallelisation removed (sequential single-rank
        surface loop, no vgen_reduce), restricted to er_method=2 /
        vel_method=1, and input handling bypasses neo_read_input.

The remaining files in that directory (tglf_c_api.f90, neo_c_api.f90, the
build_*.sh scripts and the *_inprocess.py modules) are original MITIM works
that bind by name to GACODE's public interfaces, and are covered by MITIM's
MIT License.

